              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Marathi for displeased, then the Marathi for to get fed up."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: धक्का",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "धक्का — dhakkā — \"a shock; a push\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ती बातमी ऐकून आम्हाला मोठा धक्का बसला. tī bātmī aikūn āmhālā moṭhā dhakkā baslā. Hearing that news gave us a big shock."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Masculine."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "धक्का (dhakkā) बसणे, to get a shock, with the dative; धक्का (dhakkā) देणे, to push."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "धक्का (dhakkā) is inherited from the expressive root dhakk, \"push, strike\" (CDIAL 6701), under which CDIAL lists Marathi dhakā, \"push\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for describing what you lived and felt."
            }
          ]
        },
