              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "बिथरणे — bitharṇe — \"to panic; to run wild\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "फटाक्याचा आवाज ऐकून घोडा बिथरला. phaṭākyācā āvāj aikūn ghoḍā bitharlā. The horse panicked at the sound of the firecracker."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past (he …): तो बिथरला, to bitharlā."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Of animals and people who lose their heads in fright: घोडा बिथरला, the horse bolted."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "बिथरणे (bitharṇe) is inherited by CDIAL's account: it lists Marathi bitharṇẽ, \"to misconduct oneself\", beside itharṇẽ, \"to run wild\", under Sanskrit itvara, \"walking; mean, cruel\" (CDIAL 1566). How the b- arose is not explained there, so the link is not certain."
            }
          ]
        },
